title: "Oracle Observability of Quantum Transpiler Regressions (cart)"
version: "1.2.0"
date-released: "2026-06-30"
license: MIT
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/furqan-nr/quantum-observability"
keywords:
  - quantum software engineering
  - regression test selection
  - quantum transpiler
  - Qiskit
  - test oracle
  - quantum circuit equivalence checking
abstract: >-
  cart is a research prototype and leakage-safe evaluation framework for the
  Qiskit transpiler. Its central finding is an oracle-observability gap: about
  28% of real transpiler regressions (95% Wilson CI 19-40%) corrupt internal
  contract/metadata, introduce non-determinism, or drop global phase, and are
  therefore invisible to output-equivalence oracles. It also provides a
  fault-manifestation taxonomy and a family of fault-class-matched oracles, in a
  setting where the oracle must decide circuit equivalence modulo global phase
  and qubit-layout permutation.
